INT. CORPORATE OFFICE - SEVENTH-FLOOR CONFERENCE ROOM - DAY

A glass box overlooking a parking structure. A whiteboard reads SYNERGY SPRINT in three colors of marker. A bowl of untouched fruit.

DEBORAH QUILL (40s, VP of Culture, lanyard, smile fixed) stands at the head of the table. RAJ PATWARDHAN (30s, analyst, laptop open, tie loosened) sits halfway down. CHLOE BEAUMONT (20s, intern, notebook on her knee) sits at the far end, as if hoping to be forgotten.

DEBORAH
So. We're all aligned that the new initiative is a game-changer.

RAJ
Which initiative?

DEBORAH
The one in the email.

RAJ
There were four emails.

DEBORAH
The one with the rocket emoji.

RAJ
That was a typo. It was supposed to be a calendar.

DEBORAH
The rocket stays. The rocket is the brand.

RAJ
Deborah, with respect, the rocket is a tool that reassigns three departments to a platform we have not purchased.

DEBORAH
Which is why we're being proactive.

RAJ
We are being fictional.

DEBORAH
We are being agile.

RAJ
We are being laid off. In five weeks. By the rocket.

DEBORAH
Raj, I'd love for you to hear yourself.

RAJ
I hear myself. I've heard myself since Q2. Nobody else seems to.

DEBORAH
Chloe, what do you think?

CHLOE
(barely audible)
Is the bowl of fruit for us?

DEBORAH
It's for morale.

CHLOE
It has been there since Monday.

DEBORAH
Fruit takes time to work.

RAJ
Deborah.

DEBORAH
Yes, Raj.

RAJ
I'm resigning.

DEBORAH
You can't, we have a retrospective.

RAJ
That's the best argument for it.

DEBORAH
Then let's do the retrospective first, and you can resign after as a, quote, learning.

RAJ
I'll take the fruit.

DEBORAH
Take two.

Raj picks up the bowl and walks out. Deborah stares at the door. Chloe slowly raises her hand.

CHLOE
Can I go with him?

DEBORAH
Please. Take notes.
